### 5. The Controller

A new controller to handle Request tracking specifically.

```java
package com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.Controller;

import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.ApiResponse;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.CommonRequestDto;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.PaginatedResponseDto;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.SearchRequest;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.service.CommonMasterService;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@Slf4j
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/master-requests")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class CommonRequestController {

    private final CommonMasterService service;

    /**
     * Search and Filter Master Change Requests
     * Supports filtering by status (P, A, R), creatorId, requestType, etc.
     */
    @PostMapping("/search")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<PaginatedResponseDto<CommonRequestDto>>> searchRequests(
            @RequestBody SearchRequest request) {
        log.info("Fetching master change requests with filters");
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.success(service.searchCommonRequests(request)));
    }

    /**
     * Get specific request details (including the Payload JSON)
     */
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<CommonRequestDto>> getDetails(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.success(service.getRequestById(id)));
    }
}

```

### Why this works well for you:

1. **Reuse of Logic**: By using the `GenericSpecification`, your frontend can send complex filters (e.g., "Give me all Pending requests for CGL_CODE created in the last 2 days") without you writing any extra SQL.
2. **Stateless & Standard**: It uses the same `ApiResponse` structure as your `BalanceController`, so the frontend team doesn't need to change their response parsing logic.
3. **Audit Ready**: Storing the `PAYLOAD` as a String allows you to display "Before vs After" changes easily in the UI.

